      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s probably not good to assume that there will be a valid `spi_device` (or that the given SPI device will always be at index 0.\n\nInstead, I think the SPI clock frequency should be set when `spi_enable` is called, now that the SPI clock is not based on `clock_get_apb2_freq()`. You could rename this function to:\n\n```\nvoid set_spi_frequency(uint8_t divisor)\n```\n\nand call it in `spi_enable`:\n\n```\nset_spi_frequency(spi_device-\u003ediv);\n```\n\nSee the other SPI drivers for other chips (e.g., [ST SPI](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/chip/stm32/spi_controller.c;l\u003d266-274;drc\u003d13785916328b5fbdd11fb14130ab86ee6de2b894)) for examples.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 55,
        "startChar": 21,
        "endLine": 55,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "fade76d23bb955b59b024e62b28db0e78cd498fb",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
